1 NOTE Joseph, Saint, in the New Testament, husband of the Virgin Mary. Most of
2 CONT what is known about him is contained in the first two chapters of the
2 CONT books of Matthew and Luke. Several other passages mention him as the
2 CONT father of Jesus Christ, and a few refer to him as a carpenter or an
2 CONT artisan (see Matthew 13:55; Luke 3:23; John 1:45, 6:42). He was a
2 CONT descendant of the royal line of David, and his family was from David's
2 CONT town of Bethlehem.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Joseph, Mary, and Jesus settled in Nazareth. There, Christ grew up in his
2 CONT household for 12 years. Joseph's last appearance in the Gospels occurs
2 CONT when he and Mary find the 12-year-old Jesus in the Temple (see Luke
2 CONT 2:41-51). Joseph was apparently dead by the time of Christ's passion. St.
2 CONT Joseph is venerated by both the Orthodox and Roman Catholics; he is
2 CONT regarded by the latter as the patron of the universal church. His feast
2 CONT day is March 19, in the West, and the first Sunday after Christmas, in the
2 CONT East.
